{
  "workflow": {
    "description": "To-tickets for the Gold Band instances (issue #628, wave 4): cut a spec's tickets through question rounds. A run-start gate refuses the run when the repository rule or the family allowlist forbids a bound agent. Up to three question rounds follow, unrolled and capped at three: a round that leaves a question open pauses on its manual check for the owner's answers, then the next round runs; after round three the last check hands over to the ticket draft regardless. The tickets are written as tickets.json and nothing is created in any tracker: publishing is Workflow C's publication check. No shim node has a failure edge, so a failing gate ends the run in failure.",
    "version": "0.1",
    "id": "to-tickets",
    "entry": "gate-to-tickets-start",
    "control": {
      "max_attempts": 1,
      "max_rounds": 1
    },
